# Shared Abstraction Safety

**Goal:** Do not "fix one screen" by changing code used by many screens — that creates regressions elsewhere (self-inflicted bugs).

## Shared surface (examples)

Treat as **shared** when many features depend on it:

- Shared Stimulus / JS controllers (e.g. auto-submit, tabs, confirm-delete)
- Shared view helpers / presenters used across list/index pages
- Shared concerns, base controllers, middleware, layout partials
- Shared CSS utilities / design-system classes
- Shared query/pagination helpers

If unsure: **grep call sites**. More than one consumer ⇒ shared.

## Hard rules

1. **Call-site first** — Prefer fixing the feature's view/controller/query (pass params, local options, feature-specific partial).
2. **No silent default behavior for one feature** — Do not add feature-only side effects to a shared method/controller that every consumer inherits.
3. **Opt-in if shared must change** — Use an explicit flag/value (e.g. Stimulus value, kwargs defaulting to current behavior). Default = **unchanged** for existing callers.
4. **Preserve contracts** — Shared APIs keep backward-compatible defaults; document any behavior change and list affected call sites.
5. **Blast-radius check before edit** — Grep consumers; if ≥2 screens/features, stop and choose call-site or opt-in.

## Anti-patterns (do not)

| Anti-pattern | Why it breaks |
|---|---|
| Add feature-specific cleanup/guard inside a shared submit/helper | Every form/page suddenly changes |
| Change shared pagination helper defaults for one index | Other lists lose filters or page state |
| "While here" extend shared CSS/controller for one modal | Visual/behavior regressions elsewhere |
| Copy-paste a second shared helper instead of call-site fix | Drift and duplicate bugs |
| Feature footer sets `.ahm-modal-button-*:hover` to **identical** default colors | Shared hover looks “broken” on that screen only — fix with real hover tokens or remove override |
| Feature-only side effect inside shared `turbo:before-stream-render` without chaining | Other listeners (Preline, replace-buttons) stop working |

## Preferred patterns

| Need | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Keep filters on pagination links | Pass `q` / `status` / … in **that** list's `pagination` params |
| Reset page when filters change | Omit `page` from the filter form (GET only sends form fields), or clear page **only** in that form |
| One-off DOM behavior | Feature controller / local `data-action`, not shared controller |
| Rare shared enhancement | Opt-in value/flag; default off |
| Pointer + hover on modal buttons | Additive `cursor: pointer` on shared `.ahm-modal-button` OK; hover colors via tokens (`surface` / `text-heading`). Fix no-op feature footer `:hover` overrides at **call-site CSS** |
| Re-enable UI after Turbo stream | Feature `turbo:before-stream-render` wrap that **chains** prior `event.detail.render` |

## Review checklist

Before merging a change to shared code:

- [ ] Grepped consumers (count / list)
- [ ] Default behavior unchanged for existing callers **or** explicitly opt-in
- [ ] Fix verified on **at least one other** consumer screen, not only the target feature
- [ ] No feature name / one-off business rule embedded in the shared module

## Severity

Violations that change shared defaults without opt-in → treat as **🟠 High** (cross-screen regression risk).
